      <section class="section-faq">
        <div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container-1280 w-container">
          <div class="faq-wrapper">
            <div class="left_side-faq">
              <div class="header-faq">
                <div class="text_heading-faq">
                  <div class="text-12-caps opacity-60">Frequently asked questions</div>
                  <div class="max-w-400">
                    <h2 class="h2"><span class="span">Got questions?</span> <br>We&#x27;ve got answers</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">We want to make sure you feel confident that our service is right for you. Here we’ve looked to address some commonly asked questions. If you have any more specific questions, don’t hesitate to get in touch with a member of the team.</p>
              </div><img src="/images/Frame-1707478606_4.avif" loading="lazy" alt="An abstract digital interface featuring a dark theme with various input fields, a progress bar, and a question mark icon, suggesting a user-friendly design for a software application." class="image-faq">
            </div>
            <div class="right_side-faq">
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" data-w-id="77047380-cda2-6192-4995-cd70f47c6fe7" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <h3 class="text-14-150">What is a credit?</h3>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="77047380-cda2-6192-4995-cd70f47c6feb" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">One credit is 30 minutes of design and production work. Buy a balance upfront and spend it on whatever you need, whenever you need it. Only the work itself draws down credits.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" data-w-id="1ae8d72d-6354-94a2-f3b8-ab1aedf99543" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <h3 class="text-14-150">Do meetings and calls use credits?</h3>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="1ae8d72d-6354-94a2-f3b8-ab1aedf99547" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">No. Kickoff calls, scoping discussions, feedback sessions and anything else that involves talking rather than making are free. You are only charged for work that ends up in the file.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" data-w-id="e1c852b2-e8c9-a99e-3ff0-b4373a246361" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <h3 class="text-14-150">How do we know what a piece will cost before we commit?</h3>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="e1c852b2-e8c9-a99e-3ff0-b4373a246365" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">We scope it with you first. You bring the brief, we talk it through, and your project manager comes back with a credit cost before anyone starts. That conversation costs nothing, so you always see the number before you approve it.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" data-w-id="157f6caf-4e18-0976-344a-f3c64095c625" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <h3 class="text-14-150">Do credits expire?</h3>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="157f6caf-4e18-0976-344a-f3c64095c629" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">No. It is a one time payment and your balance stays until you use it. That is the point of the model, since it lets you commit budget before a quarter closes and spend it at your own pace.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" data-w-id="4e40c6ff-70c9-8722-7205-1e12c0741c35" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <h3 class="text-14-150">Which plan should we buy?</h3>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="4e40c6ff-70c9-8722-7205-1e12c0741c39" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">Starter at 1,000 credits is the baseline. Growth at 2,000 brings the rate to $16 and saves $4,000 against buying the same volume at Starter rates. Enterprise at 4,000 or more brings it to $13 and saves over $20,000. Buy the tier your annual volume actually reaches, because the rate is where the value sits.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <h3 class="text-14-150">What happens when we run out?</h3>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="ffc88df0-1593-d473-f22f-ea6dcd6219ec" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">You top up. Starter and Growth top up at $18 per credit and Enterprise tops up at $13. Worth knowing that Growth tops up above its own effective rate, so if you expect to run past 2,000 credits it is cheaper to buy the larger balance upfront.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <h3 class="text-14-150">How is this different from the subscription?</h3>
